<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27437" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">măcellārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		macellum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				meat-market</i> or <i>provision-market</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">taberna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 3, 4, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">negotiator artis macellariae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 647, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ARS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4302</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">măcellārĭus</span></b> ,
				ĭi, m., <i>a
				meat-seller, victualler</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vendere apros macellario,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 2, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 4, 2</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 26</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">macellarios adjuvare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Vesp. 19</span></i>
			.</div>
